Child custody-sex offense conviction
HB0083
presumption.
Sponsored By: Representative(s) Pendergraft, Angelos, Brady,
Haroldson, Kelly and Knapp and Senator(s) Hutchings
AN ACT relating to domestic relations; specifying a rebuttable presumption that
no sex offender shall have unsupervised visitation with a child; requiring
consideration of sex-related convictions when considering the best interests of
a child in custody determinations upon divorce; and providing for an effective
date.
